            "Traditional cold chain governance relied on passive chemical indicator strips or retrospective USB temperature data loggers that were extracted and read only after the shipment reached its final destination. While useful for post-mortem analysis, retrospective logging is fundamentally reactive: if a refrigeration unit fails mid-flight, the cargo sits ruined for days before anyone discovers the failure. Modern digital cold chains deploy real-time Internet of Things (IoT) sensor telemetry, providing continuous, proactive visibility into environmental conditions across global transit lanes.",
