            "To accurately quantify cumulative thermal degradation, pharmaceutical scientists and logistics engineers calculate the Mean Kinetic Temperature (MKT). Formulated by Haynes in 1971 and mandated by the United States Pharmacopeia (USP Chapter 1160) and International Council for Harmonisation (ICH), MKT is defined as the single calculated temperature that, if maintained continuously over a given storage period, would produce the same total thermal degradation as the observed fluctuating temperature sequence.",
